                    <p class=MsoNormal><span style="font-family:仿宋;mso-bidi-font-family:'Times New Roman';font-size:12.0000pt;
mso-font-kerning:1.0000pt;"><font face="仿宋"><p>"Surgery A" is a course designed to systematically introduce the fundamental theories and clinical practices of surgery, covering the diagnosis and treatment principles of common surgical diseases as well as basic surgical techniques. The course emphasizes the integration of theory and practice, fostering clinical thinking and hands-on skills through case studies and practical training. It aims to lay a solid foundation for students pursuing a career in the field of surgery.</p></font></span><span style="font-family:'Times New Roman';mso-fareast-font-family:仿宋;font-size:10.5000pt;
mso-font-kerning:1.0000pt;"><o:p></o:p></span></p>
